<doxygen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="compound.xsd" version="1.18.0" xml:lang="en-US">
  <compounddef id="topics_8h" kind="file" language="C++">
    <compoundname>topics.h</compoundname>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Project specific Doxygen topics definitions. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file organises the principal Doxygen groups and documentation topics for the µTest++ Testing Framework library, which is part of the µOS++ project.</para>
<para>Although named as a header, this file is not included in the build process; it is intended exclusively as a documentation resource for Doxygen. Due to Doxygen processing requirements, it cannot be provided as a Markdown file or as a <computeroutput>.doxyfile</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>It defines the tree and the order of the documentation topics, which is also the order of the sidebar, by including with <computeroutput>@include{doc}</computeroutput> the hand-written Doxygen sources of the <computeroutput>website/doxygen</computeroutput> folder: the main page (<computeroutput>pages/</computeroutput>), the file and folder pages (<computeroutput>files/</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>folders/</computeroutput>), the topics (<computeroutput>topics/</computeroutput>, with the C++ API topics in <computeroutput>topics/cpp-api/</computeroutput>), and the configuration macros (<computeroutput>macros/</computeroutput>).</para>
<para>The text of the topics is not in this file, but in the included files; this page, for example, is <computeroutput>files/topics-h.dox</computeroutput>, whereas <computeroutput><ref refid="topics_8h" kindref="compound">topics.h</ref></computeroutput> is in the <computeroutput>website/doxygen</computeroutput> folder.  </para>
    </detaileddescription>
